WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.019
Riya asks her college placement bot: how many

2
00:00:03.088 --> 00:00:06.072
active backlogs are allowed? The answer is one

3
00:00:06.118 --> 00:00:09.567
sentence, on page four of a forty-page policy.

4
00:00:09.917 --> 00:00:12.227
But the model never reads the whole PDF.

5
00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:14.782
It only sees the few chunks you retrieve.

6
00:00:15.269 --> 00:00:17.905
So how you cut the document decides everything.

7
00:00:18.255 --> 00:00:20.484
Cut the chunks too large, and each one

8
00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:23.863
mixes many topics. Retrieval gets noisy, and you

9
00:00:23.921 --> 00:00:25.500
pay to send filler.

10
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:28.230
Cut them too small, and they lose context.

11
00:00:28.427 --> 00:00:30.691
It must be cleared before the drive. What

12
00:00:30.738 --> 00:00:31.841
is it?

13
00:00:32.191 --> 00:00:34.292
So start at around five hundred tokens per

14
00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:36.858
chunk. But a fixed cut can slice Riya's

15
00:00:36.893 --> 00:00:39.285
sentence in half, and neither chunk holds the

16
00:00:39.343 --> 00:00:40.318
answer.

17
00:00:40.668 --> 00:00:43.849
The fix is overlap. Repeat about fifty tokens

18
00:00:43.965 --> 00:00:45.416
from the end of one chunk at the

19
00:00:45.451 --> 00:00:46.937
start of the next.

20
00:00:47.287 --> 00:00:49.377
Now the sentence survives whole in at least

21
00:00:49.435 --> 00:00:52.709
one chunk. Better still, split on paragraphs and

22
00:00:52.779 --> 00:00:55.321
sentences, not character counts.

23
00:00:55.671 --> 00:00:58.156
Give every chunk an ID card: the file

24
00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.501
name and the page number. That becomes your

25
00:01:00.559 --> 00:01:02.173
citation later.

26
00:01:02.523 --> 00:01:05.739
Then measure. Chunk the same PDF three ways,

27
00:01:05.902 --> 00:01:08.131
ask the same questions, and keep the one

28
00:01:08.154 --> 00:01:10.418
that retrieves the right passage.

29
00:01:10.768 --> 00:01:14.959
Remember this: bad chunking ruins good models. Start

30
00:01:15.006 --> 00:01:17.362
at five hundred tokens with fifty of overlap,

31
00:01:17.479 --> 00:01:18.663
then measure.

32
00:01:19.013 --> 00:01:22.310
Next lesson: the full RAG pipeline, with citations.
